<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Winterthur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Winterthur is a city in the Swiss canton of Zürich, north-east of the city of Zürich, and the canton's second largest town. In 919 Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burchard-ii-duke-of-swabia">Burchard II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a> defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-ii-of-burgundy">Rudolf II of Upper Burgundy</a> near the town. Held by the counts of Kyburg and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, it passed to Zürich in 1467 and grew into an important centre of engineering and textiles in the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/winterthur.jpg" alt="Winterthur" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JoachimKohler-HB · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blick_auf_die_Winterthurer_Altstadt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
